Vita: borealis::net reports "unavailable", as upstream already does for the Switch.
The Vita has no socket service started (SceNet/SceNetCtl are not initialized by the
port), so connect()/listen() fail through upstream's own available() == false path;
endpoint parsing stays upstream. Not game code.

--- a/src/net/platform_posix.cpp
+++ b/src/net/platform_posix.cpp
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 namespace borealis::net::detail::platform {
 
 bool available() noexcept {
-#if defined(__SWITCH__)
+#if defined(__SWITCH__) || defined(__vita__)
     return false;
 #else
     return true;
